From 1a83610b4fe1dee9547d1728e768f0068eb81853 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <reaper@localhost>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 18:47:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 243/245] audit batches B/C/D/E: rwarden, reaper_skip, i18n,
 samba stamp

Batch B (rc/rwarden.c):
- C5 (LAN subnet %%) is a FALSE POSITIVE - the %% is an fprintf escape that
  emits a single % in the generated shell (${LANIP%.*} -> 192.168.50.0/24,
  verified). Left unchanged; changing it would emit a malformed %. conversion.
- L2 (real, currently active): moved the LAN-source anti-lockout RETURN to
  AFTER the outbound dst-drop rules so a LAN client reaching a blocked dst is
  actually enforced (an early LAN RETURN exempted all LAN-sourced forwarded
  traffic, silently disabling outbound blocking).
- C6: geo update now builds into rw_geo_tmp and swaps only if non-empty (mirrors
  the threat feed), so a transient fetch failure keeps the last-good country set
  instead of the old flush-before-fetch fail-open.

Batch C (httpd/reaper_inject.c): added error_page.htm, offline.htm,
gotoHomePage.htm and blocking.asp to reaper_skip[] so WAN-outage / block pages
render instead of bouncing an unauthenticated client to the login (C4 + L1).

Batch D (www/*.dict): C7 - overwrote the RQOS_117 tooltip in all 24 non-EN
dicts with the correct EN text in place (the translated "enter ~90%" guidance
double-derated the download cap to ~81%). C8 - seeded the 43 EN RWDN_ (Warden)
strings into all 24 non-EN dicts after RGK_60 (English placeholders, order
matching EN). Native translation of RQOS_117 + RWDN_ is a follow-up i18n pass.

Batch E (samba-4.15.13/build-reaper.sh): the build stamp now stores a sha256 of
reaper-patches/ and the skip check compares it, so a patch add/change forces a
rebuild instead of reshipping a stale binary with the Reaper suffix but without
the current CVE patches (C33).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
